Package: test2infeR
Type: Package
Title: HMM Inference for Longitudinal Diagnostic Test Data
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Arthur", "Newbury", email = "a.r.newbury@exeter.ac.uk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R interface to a Julia-based Hidden Markov Model (HMM) inference
    engine for longitudinal diagnostic testing data. Latent infection status is
    inferred on a regular time grid from imperfect test results, with test
    sensitivity and specificity either held fixed or estimated. Supports MAP,
    MLE and NUTS, configurable year-effect processes, and selection of a subset
    of tests. The package can install Julia and instantiate a pinned Julia
    project automatically.
